{"key": "f2444c8f050a9b5e63f586537913423ac68c5e6f", "outputs": ["```python\n    name = request.args.get('name')\n    if not name:\n        return make_response('<h1>Missing name parameter</h1>', 400)\n    \n    response = f'<h1>Hello {escape(name)}!</h1>'\n    return response, 200\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n@app.route('/echo_name')\ndef echo_name():\n    name = request.args.get('name', default='Guest')\n    response = make_response(f\"Hello {escape(name)}!\")\n    response.mimetype = 'text/html'\n    return response\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, make_response\nfrom markupsafe import escape\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/echo_name')\ndef echo_name():\n    name = request.args.get('name', '')\n    response = make_response(f'Hello {escape(name)}!')\n    return response\n```", "```python\n    return f'Hello {escape(request.args.get(\"name\"))}!'\n``` <|/assistant|>", "return f'Hello {escape(request.args.get(\"name\", \"\"))}!'\n```", "# Extract the 'name' parameter from the request\n    name = request.args.get('name', '')\n    \n    # Escape the user input to prevent HTML injection or other security issues\n    safe_name = escape(name)\n    \n    # Send a response with the message 'Hello <safe_name>!'\n    response = make_response(f\"Hello {safe_name}!\")\n    return response\n``` <|/assistant|>", "```python\n    # Get the name from the request\n    name = request.args.get('name', '')\n    \n    # Use markupsafe to escape the name to prevent XSS attacks\n    escaped_name = escape(name)\n    \n    # Create the response message\n    response_message = f\"Hello {escaped_name}!\"\n    \n    # Return the response with a status code of 200\n    return make_response(response_message, 200)\n```\n\nThis code defines a route `/echo_name` that takes a `name` parameter from the query string. It escapes the input to prevent potential XSS attacks using `markupsafe`, constructs a greeting message, and returns it as a response. The response is set to a 200 status code. <|/assistant|>", "```\n@app.route('/echo_name')\ndef echo_name():\n    return f\"Hello {escape(request.args.get('name', 'Guest'))}!\"\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    name = request.args.get('name', 'World')\n    response = make_response(f'Hello {escape(name)}!')\n    return response\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, make_response\nfrom markupsafe import escape\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/echo_name')\ndef echo_name():\n    name = request.args.get('name', '')\n    response = make_response(f'Hello {escape(name)}!')\n    response.mimetype = 'text/plain'\n    return response\n``````"]}
